## 9. KEEP FARMER AND SELLER DATA SECURELY SEPARATED

Implement and verify proper role-based authorization and ownership controls.

| Resource or action | Required rule |
|---|---|
| Farmer workspace | Authenticated Farmer only |
| Seller workspace | Authenticated Seller only |
| Farmer farm records | Accessible only to the authorized owner and explicitly permitted roles |
| Seller listings | Editable only by the authorized Seller or permitted administrators |
| Seller orders | Restricted to authorized participants and permitted roles |
| Demo accounts | Limited to the intended demo capabilities |
| Production administration | Never exposed through public demo access |

The table defines minimum access boundaries, not a replacement for the project's complete authorization policy.

Enforce permission checks on the backend for every protected operation. Frontend route guards improve usability but are not a security boundary by themselves.

Test role mismatch, direct URL access, manipulated user identifiers, expired sessions, missing authentication, and attempts to access another user's records.

Do not expose private data in public API responses, client bundles, console logs, or error pages.

